    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46703" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭperfĭcĭārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>situated on another man</i>'<i>s land</i>, <i>superficiary</i> (jurid. Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					10, 2, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					43, 18, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mathematice, ut ita dicam, superficiaria est:
					in alieno aedificat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 88, 28</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭper-fĭcĭārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>one who has a
				house on another man</i>'<i>s land</i>, <i>a superficiary</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 6, 1,
				74</span></i>; <i><span class="en">39, 2,
			18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">43, 17, 3</span></i>
			<i>med.</i> al.</div>
